<!--
  Published URLs, which are not the repo's paths: the Pages workflow copies games/* back to
  the site root before uploading, so games/2048/play.html is served at /artivy/2048/play.html.
  Write the served path here, never the repo path.

  Every URL here is under /artivy/, which is this sitemap's own directory. The domain root
  is a different repo and has its own sitemap.xml beside its robots.txt — cross-submitting it
  from here is legal but pointlessly ambiguous, and ambiguity is not worth one URL.

  The game pages are listed in their directory form, without index.html, because that is
  what each page's own rel=canonical declares. A sitemap that disagreed with the canonical
  would hand Google two answers to the same question.

  selftest.html is left out on purpose. It is a developer harness that prints pass/fail lines
  for each game's rules, and it carries a noindex tag of its own — nothing about it belongs in
  a search result.
-->
